# SIM / operational clock (GUARDRAILS §5.3)

Any work that uses a **date, time, “today”, duration, overdue check, or operator-visible timestamp** must honour the amber **SIM TIME** bar.

## Use

- Instant “now”: `operationalNowIso()` / `operationalNowMs()` / `resolveOperationalNow()` from `src/lib/operational-clock.ts` (or `operational-time.ts`)
- Calendar today: `todayLocalIso()` / `getOperationalTodayIso()` / `useOperationalTodayIso()`
- Weekday for schedules: `todaysSydneyDayCode()` only after a SIM-aware today hook so the UI re-renders when SIM changes

## Do not

- `new Date()`, `new Date().toISOString()`, or `.toISOString().slice(0, 10)` for floor stamps or “today”
- Manifest depart / arrive / board, check-in/out, open/close, Off today, run live-status, roster dates, trip_date, sweeps, curfew

## Wall-clock exception only

- `operational_ledger.created_at` (DB default) and outbox `savedAt` (when the device queued a write)
- If the **operator will see the time on a screen**, it is not this exception

Production builds use the same helpers (live clock). Never special-case TEST with a second clock.
